            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I absolutely loved the outcome of this, but in my mind 1/4 cup of minced garlic and 2 cans of chicken broth was SO unnecessary and excessive. As the recipe suggests, I used minced garlic to taste, probably a third of what was called for, and only enough chicken broth necessary to allow the bok choy to steam. I poured enough broth into my large skillet to a depth of about 1/2 inch. Otherwise a great, basic reference recipe for cooking whole baby bok choy, one I know I'll come back to."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Barbiejb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious. I used two large garlic cloves, and decreased the broth as others suggested. I only cooked the garlic for 1 minute to avoid it becoming bitter. The whole baby Bok choy made a nice presentation and is perfect for a dinner party, but for weeknight family dinners i might try chopping the Bok choy before cooking.",
            "datePublished": "2016-10-25T02:26:01.140Z"
          },
